  "body": "I know I know I know, it's old and broken, or at least that's the consensus among those who used it way back when, but I recently discovered `document.all` in an effort to find more direct ways of referencing elements with an id attribute and I love it! Works great for a little side project. \r\n\r\nThe DX is nice:\r\n```\r\n<span id=\"welcomeMessage\" hidden>Welcome!</span>\r\n\r\ndocument.all.welcomeMessage.hidden = false;\r\nvs.\r\ndocument.getElementById('welcomeMessage').hidden = false;\r\n```\r\nAfter learning more about some of the history and problems, I'm hoping `all` can be patched. Chrome team actually did some work on it in the not too distant past, so maybe there's hope?\r\n\r\nIs it feasible to fix `document.all`? If not, what about a `document.forms` for elements with an id?",
